{
  "program": "CBTRN03C",
  "caseId": "case18",
  "description": "Three accounts, unequal amounts and a negative in the middle, so no two totals in the report can be confused with one another. Each account break writes the account total accumulated since the previous break and zeroes it at :310, while the page total keeps accumulating across all three accounts and is rolled into the grand total once, at end of file. The middle account's total is therefore negative and prints with '-' through the + mask, the third account's total is never written, and the grand total equals the arithmetic sum of every amount plus the last one counted twice - which is the only value consistent with both defect 2 and the single roll-up site at :297.",
